meta {
  name: Delete Patient Completely (Full Purge)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patients/code/{{patientCode}}/full-delete
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  patientCode: CHANGE_ME_2600055967
}

tests {
  test("patient is fully purged", function() {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  IRREVERSIBLE. Permanently deletes the patient identified by patientCode, along with every
  examination, DICOM instance, AI analysis/result, diagnosis review, report, and RAG knowledge
  index entry that exists only because of that patient. Physical files (.dcm, preview/annotated/
  ROI/GradCAM images, report PDF) are deleted from disk on a best-effort basis after the database
  changes succeed.

  Set the patientCode var above to a real, disposable patient code before running this - do not
  run it against patientCode 2600055967 (or any real patient) unless you actually intend to
  destroy that record. There is no confirmation step and no undo.

  Unlike every other write endpoint in this collection, this one has no role/permission
  requirement beyond a valid access token: run any login request first (Login Success for admin,
  Login Doctor for a doctor account) - either will work here.
}
